# SLASH-LEADING-WS: the three drafts the unit was asked about, as typed --
# `  /he`, a line break then `/he`, and `say /he`. fx lists /shell for `he`
# (a substring of its name), which xfx does not have until C8 lands (the
# ledger's cause for fx's /shell rows), so p5-slash-leading-ws asks for
# `/help` instead; this one keeps the words.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
wait 3
type   /he
wait 0.6
snap spaces
key C-u
wait 0.3
key C-j
type /he
wait 0.6
snap newline
key Tab
wait 0.5
key C-u
wait 0.3
type say /he
wait 0.6
snap mid
